1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Alex: The clean-checkout workflow starts with versioned inputs.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
Morgan: That makes the extraction example reliable on a new machine.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,500
Alex: The PDF, document, presentation, and image are all synthetic.

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,000
Morgan: Good. We should never use an invoice or internal slide deck as a fixture.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,500
Alex: The checksum test will catch accidental binary changes.

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,000
Morgan: The runtime matrix also proves that file paths are flow-relative.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,500
Alex: Offline examples run without network access or credentials.

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,000
Morgan: Service-backed examples remain documented but are classified separately.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Alex: Generated files belong in an isolated temporary directory.

10
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:35,000
Morgan: That prevents examples from overwriting their own source fixtures.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,500
Alex: Small assets keep the repository fast to clone and easy to inspect.

12
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,000
Morgan: Now every example can state its real prerequisites clearly.
